{"title":"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Spot's doghouse has a regular hexagonal base that measures one yard on each side. He is tethered to a vertex with a two-yard rope. What is the area, in square yards, of the region outside of the doghouse that Spot can reach?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/9/5f9941cb210b725591b49027e2b6fa081ae9227a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 2\\pi/3 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 2\\pi \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 5\\pi/2 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 8\\pi/3 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 3\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"439\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/bad420f7af2fcfd838497541439db8b99a1dceba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(polygon(6)); draw(Arc((1/2,sqrt(3)/2),2,-60,180)); draw(Arc((-1/2,sqrt(3)/2),1,180,240)); draw(Arc((1,0),1,240,300)); draw((-1/2,sqrt(3)/2)--(-3/2,sqrt(3)/2), dotted); draw((1,0)--(3/2,-sqrt(3)/2),dotted); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"245\" /></center>\n<p>Part of what Spot can reach is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f657e14f27bbaa0d2ad78498cfc311dd6d871cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{240}{360}=\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"67\" height=\"37\" /> of a circle with radius 2, which \ngives him <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/d/9dd6a3b4057e5ad2da7c419a4127e80893320b06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"22\" height=\"37\" />. He can also reach two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/9/399554977540e3d6e1753c36f9c74478caffcdb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{60}{360}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" /> parts of a unit circle, which combines to give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d2d0dc818ffa40c824ec87c9ad9c51fa86f458d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" />. The total area is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5d4a39c601726949a5cfde4a9bbd8d30a64fb56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\pi$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6c182d936b9ff33cadf7f6e3391eeddf9248a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"36\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We can clearly see that the area must be more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/d/9dd6a3b4057e5ad2da7c419a4127e80893320b06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"22\" height=\"37\" />, and the only such answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6c182d936b9ff33cadf7f6e3391eeddf9248a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"36\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lkk3SAjsPaI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lkk3SAjsPaI</a>  ~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/C2pNSPfTxgA\">https://youtu.be/C2pNSPfTxgA</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A\">2002 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1